            "partial": true,
            "distractorPenalty": 0,
            "explanation": "The strip has to happen before the length is measured, or the spaces get counted. None of these methods change the string in place — they hand back a new one, which is why line 2 stores the result back in name. upper() and lower() are only printed, so the tidied name is left as it was.",
